From: Draftway
Subject: [MV2] Do not treat MV2 extensions as deprecated

ungoogled-chromium's extensions-manifestv2.patch already stops Chromium from
blocking or disabling Manifest V2 extensions (ShouldDisableLegacyExtensions()
returns false). manifest_v2_util::IsExtensionAffected() still reports every
non-component MV2 extension as "affected", which drives the leftover
deprecation UI, developerPrivate flags and metrics. Make it return false.

webRequestBlocking needs no change: _permission_features.json grants it to
MV2 extensions without a location restriction.

Category: 40-mv2. Drop when upstream removes manifest_v2_util.
---
--- a/extensions/browser/manifest_v2_util.cc	2026-10-23 13:44:21.666849805 +0200
+++ b/extensions/browser/manifest_v2_util.cc	2026-10-23 13:44:36.265827911 +0200
@@ -20,28 +20,12 @@
 bool IsExtensionAffected(int manifest_version,
                          Manifest::Type manifest_type,
                          mojom::ManifestLocation manifest_location) {
-  // Only extensions < MV3.
-  if (manifest_version >= 3) {
-    return false;
-  }
-
-  // Only extensions (not platform apps, etc). User scripts are treated as
-  // extensions for the sake of APIs and in presentation to the user, so we
-  // include them here.
-  if (manifest_type != Manifest::Type::kExtension &&
-      manifest_type != Manifest::Type::kLoginScreenExtension &&
-      manifest_type != Manifest::Type::kUserScript) {
-    return false;
-  }
-
-  // Ignore component extensions (they're implementation details of Chrome).
-  if (Manifest::IsComponentLocation(manifest_location)) {
-    return false;
-  }
-
-  // The extension is an MV2 (or lower) extension; we should warn the user
-  // about it.
-  return true;
+  // Draftway: Manifest V2 is a supported extension format in this browser
+  // (see ungoogled-chromium's extensions-manifestv2.patch, which already keeps
+  // MV2 extensions enabled). Report no extension as affected by the upstream
+  // MV2 deprecation, so no deprecation warnings, badges or Safety Hub
+  // recommendations are shown for MV2 extensions.
+  return false;
 }
 
 }  // namespace extensions::manifest_v2_util
